ls":68.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.09705009887664019,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":86.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.036331469557881274,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":54.6,"_gate_piotroski":9,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":100.0,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.01565588745847224,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":46.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.09275379685858298,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":71.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.020217017891758757,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":33.6,"_gate_share_shrink":0.022354535583583912,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":22.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.019970951343500364,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":66.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.110740006,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":73.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Nasdaq, Inc. operates as a technology company that serves capital markets and other industries in the United States and internationally. It operates through three segments: Capital Access Platforms, Financial Technology, and Market Services. The company distributes historical and real-time market data; develops and licenses Nasdaq-branded indices and financial products; provides investor relations intelligence, governance solutions, and sustainability solution products for public and private companies, and organizations, as well as insights and workflow solutions; and operates listing platforms. It also offers Verafin, a cloud-based platform to detect, investigate, and report money laundering and financial frauds; AxiomSL, a risk data management and regulatory reporting solution; cloud-enabled and on-premises surveillance solutions to assist in complying with market rules, regulations, and internal market surveillance policies; Calypso, a platform providing cross-asset, front-to-back trading, treasury, risk, and collateral management solutions; and trade management and colocation services, as well as handles assets comprising cash equities, equity derivatives, currencies, various interest-bearing securities, commodities, energy products, and digital currencies. In addition, the company provides equity derivative trading and clearing, cash equity trading and fixed income, currency and commodities trading, and fixed income trading and clearing services, as well as tape plan data services; operates various exchanges, including derivatives, commodities, cash equity, debt, structured products, and exchange traded products; and offers clearing, settlement, and central depository services. The company was formerly known as The NASDAQ OMX Group, Inc. and changed its name to Nasdaq, Inc. in September 2015. Nasdaq, Inc. was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Adena T. Friedman | CEO & Chairman | Age 55 | Compensation: $7.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $861K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $207K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Nasdaq, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $60.2B market cap on $8.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 59% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $2.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 44% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4437329030944256},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (46% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 9/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Nasdaq (NDAQ) Faces A Fresh Test Following Q3 Revenue Growth And 23 5 Trading Plans","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-ndaq/nasdaq/news/nasdaq-ndaq-faces-a-fresh-test-following-q3-revenue-growth-a","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794526465.143,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.807,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"How Nasdaq Inc. (NDAQ) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/How_Nasdaq_Inc._NDAQ_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111226041401_1794518041.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794518041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Analyzing Nasdaq (NASDAQ:NDAQ) & Resolute Holdings Management (NYSE:RHLD)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelin